  System.LibC.C.adam - the pure C routines of libc.a, Adam's own C library
  (res/libs/vendor/<triple>/libc.a, built by AdamLang-Libs from upstream
  musl v1.2.6, MIT license, with the same flags for every target, so a
  routine gives the same result on win64 and linux64), written by `adam
  cimport` from the math.h and string.h it is built with
  (res/libs/vendor/include/c) with the header's own names: the math, then
  the byte-string routines that only touch the caller's memory (memcpy,
  strlen ..); ctype and the conversions join it when a job needs them. The
  OS-facing C (malloc / free, FILE stdio, errno, threads, time, exit)
  stays the platform's own C runtime and is not declared here. Left out
  (the spec's [skip]): every long double form, as Adam has no long double;
  the type-generic macros (fpclassify, isnan ..) and their helpers, musl's
  __fpclassify / __signbit (renamed on win64, where mingw-w64 owns those
  names) and FP_NAN .. FP_NORMAL with them; the string routines libc.a
  does not build (strdup, strtok, the locale's and the BSD ones) with the
  locale's type; NULL (Adam has nil). Do not edit: a change belongs in the
  spec, res/cimport/System.LibC.C.cimport.toml, then regenerate.
*******************************************************************************/

